  "scope_and_limits": [
    "RuntimeType::register_owned and register_owned_with_interfaces share the registry with legacy register, preserve first-live-registration metadata, own the parent handle, and unbind only their own registry entry at final drop.",
    "Class macros retain one owned descriptor handle in their static OnceLock; generic class descriptors retain one handle in the static owner cache.",
    "The legacy borrowed register path preserves zero initial descriptor count but pins its allocation for process lifetime; this compatibility path does not reproduce raw-pointer destruction.",
    "The registry uses Rust TypeId rather than C++ type_info name strings; cross-module TypeId identity is not separately proven here.",
    "Native destructor lookup races are not probed because OCCT's destructor unbind is not protected by the registration mutex; Rust registry mutation is synchronized."
  ]
